p__bar"></span><svg class="hdraw" viewBox="0 0 92 62" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M26.0 16.0 Q24.5 34.5 24.1 52.1" stroke="#B0ACA2" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M26.0 16.0 Q24.5 34.5 24.1 52.1" stroke="#B0ACA2" stroke-width="1.3299999999999998" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="0.38" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M41.0 16.0 Q41.0 33.8 41.2 51.8" stroke="#B0ACA2" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M41.0 16.0 Q41.0 33.8 41.2 51.8" stroke="#B0ACA2" stroke-width="1.3299999999999998" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="0.38" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M56.0 16.0 Q55.8 33.4 56.3 51.6" stroke="#B0ACA2" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M56.0 16.0 Q55.8 33.4 56.3 51.6" stroke="#B0ACA2" stroke-width="1.3299999999999998" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="0.38" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M65.5 34.1 Q65.5 39.1 65.9 42.0 Q63.4 46.8 59.4 50.7 Q57.2 54.4 55.4 59.1 Q49.8 58.9 45.8 59.1 Q41.3 57.9 34.5 58.6 Q30.1 56.0 26.3 54.5 Q22.9 53.3 18.8 50.5 Q17.9 48.3 15.6 45.1 Q16.5 40.5 15.4 35.0 Q16.2 30.5 15.1 26.8 Q19.0 23.5 20.4 18.3 Q24.2 15.7 28.4 11.1 Q31.4 9.7 36.5 7.8 Q40.0 8.6 43.1 9.5 Q48.7 11.0 53.6 12.2 Q58.3 15.0 60.6 16.2 Q64.4 19.9 65.6 22.7 Q66.4 28.7 65.8 34.8" stroke="#DA0007" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/><path class="hd" pathLength="1" d="M65.5 34.1 Q65.5 39.1 65.9 42.0 Q63.4 46.8 59.4 50.7 Q57.2 54.4 55.4 59.1 Q49.8 58.9 45.8 59.1 Q41.3 57.9 34.5 58.6 Q30.1 56.0 26.3 54.5 Q22.9 53.3 18.8 50.5 Q17.9 48.3 15.6 45.1 Q16.5 40.5 15.4 35.0 Q16.2 30.5 15.1 26.8 Q19.0 23.5 20.4 18.3 Q24.2 15.7 28.4 11.1 Q31.4 9.7 36.5 7.8 Q40.0 8.6 43.1 9.5 Q48.7 11.0 53.6 12.2 Q58.3 15.0 60.6 16.2 Q64.4 19.9 65.6 22.7 Q66.4 28.7 65.8 34.8" stroke="#DA0007" stroke-width="1.1199999999999999" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="0.38" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/></svg><p class="jstep__d">Today</p><p class="jstep__t">Three to one</p><p class="jstep__x">Every mandate runs the same way. Three names, all hireable, and the reasoning behind each rank.</p></div></div>
  <p class="fn__line" data-rv>Everyone else was shipping. We were <em>still reading</em>.</p>
</div></section>



<section class="wrap band" id="believe">
  <div class="shead">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--red" data-rv>What we hold to</p>
      <h2 class="h2" data-rv style="--d:60ms">Four things, and we argue about the rest.</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="dek" data-rv style="--d:100ms">These are not values on a wall. <b>Each one cost us something
    to hold</b>: a shortcut we could have taken, a number that would have looked better.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bels" data-rv style="--d:140ms"><div class="bel"><span class="bel__n">01</span><p class="bel__t">No candidate is bad.</p><p class="bel__x">There is a yes for you and a no somewhere else, and it is usually the same person. Fit isn’t quality: it’s the manager, the project, the people they’d sit beside.</p></div><div class="bel"><span class="bel__n">02</span><p class="bel__t">The reject is always human.</p><p class="bel__x">The engine surfaces and explains. It can’t turn anyone down. A person reads the transcript, a person writes the verdict, and you make the call.</p></div><div class="bel"><span class="bel__n">03</span><p class="bel__t">Judgment evaporates unless you write it down.</p><p class="bel__x">A good conversation disappears the moment it ends unless someone records what they heard, why it mattered, and where the doubt remains. The next brief should begin with that reasoning, not another hunch.</p></div><div class="bel"><span class="bel__n">04</span><p class="bel__t">Both sides get checked.</p><p class="bel__x">A candidate proving themselves to a company that has proved nothing is not a conversation. Before a request reaches anyone, the team on the other end clears its own set of checks.</p></div></div>
  <div class="argue" data-rv>
    <p class="argue__k">And one we have not settled</p>
    <p class="argue__q">How long should we keep a transcript?</p>
    <div class="argue__g">
      <div class="argue__i"><p class="argue__w">Abhishek</p>
        <p class="argue__x">Keep them. The whole argument for writing judgment down is that the tenth
        search starts from the previous nine. Purge the record and you have built a faster tool, not a
        deeper file.</p></div>
      <div class="argue__i"><p class="argue__w">Akshata</p>
        <p class="argue__x">Not indefinitely. A transcript is a person on a particular afternoon, and
        holding it for years means someone is judged in 2029 on a bad half hour in 2026. They should be
        able to make it go away.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="argue__ft">Today it is a defined clock and then purged, which is Akshata’s answer. We keep
    written judgment long enough to improve the next brief, not long enough to let an old half hour define
    someone forever. We have moved the date twice and we will probably move it again.</p>
  </div>
</section>



<section class="trust band" id="name"><div class="wrap">
